The bug occurs because the volume up, down, and mute keypresses are reported through both the Panasonic ACPI HKEY interface and the PS/2 keyboard interface (atkbd device). The code does not filter out the duplicate keypresses from the atkbd device, leading to multiple reports of the same keypress event.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
switch (data & 0x7f) {
    case 0x20: /* e0 20 / e0 a0, Volume Mute press / release */
    case 0x2e: /* e0 2e / e0 ae, Volume Down press / release */
    case 0x30: /* e0 30 / e0 b0, Volume Up press / release */
        return true;
}
```
Reason:
These code statements filter out the specific keypress events for volume mute, down, and up by returning `true` when these keypresses are detected. This prevents the duplicate keypress events from being reported to the system, effectively resolving the issue of unintended behavior caused by the duplicate reports.

